      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ParameterOrder.lean",
      "rule": "R7",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "Returning success after finding an unresolved name lets later resolution report the wrong error: `CHECK(abs(1,2) + nosuch + ?)` reports an argument-count error in the model, but SQLite 3.51.0 reports `no such column: nosuch`. Fix: preserve and return the first name-resolution error, with a regression test."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261023T055459Z-a78a1092#2",
      "line": 31,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ParameterOrder.lean",
      "rule": "R7",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The left-first comparison traversal predicts a prohibited parameter for `CHECK(? IS nosuch)`, but SQLite resolves the right-hand identifier first and reports `no such column: nosuch`. Fix: implement SQLite’s special resolution order for `IS` and `IS NOT` and test both operators."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261023T055459Z-a78a1092#3",
      "line": 36,
      "path": "packages/belay-sqlite-model/Belay/Sqlite/Model/Resolution/ParameterOrder.lean",
      "rule": "R7",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "Scanning the operand of an empty `IN` list introduces a regression: `CHECK(nosuch IN () + ?)` now reports a missing column, while SQLite eliminates the empty-list expression and reports the prohibited parameter. Fix: account for expressions SQLite eliminates before name resolution and add regression coverage."
    }
  ],
